ATAK-CIV navigation icons
-------------------------

The right-hand navigation menu ships sixteen icons adapted from ATAK-CIV.

Source:   ATAK-CIV 5.5.1.10
          commit 9f6893dd657feacc35ec5de03dad721c2e44170e
          ("Merge branch 'upstream/5.5.1.10'")
          atak/ATAK/app/src/main/res/drawable-xxxhdpi/
          atak/ATAK/app/src/main/res/drawable-hdpi/   (missions only)

License:  GNU General Public License v3.0

Form:     The original raster assets were traced to SVG. The rasters retained
          for provenance are under branding/atak-icons/primary/ and the traced
          SVGs under branding/atak-icons/svg-traced/. The path data is embedded
          in api/web/src/base/taknz-nav-icons.ts. No pixels of the originals are
          distributed in the built application; the traced outlines are
          derivative works of them and are covered by the same license.

ATAK-CIV states in its README.md and INTENT.md that contributions by US Federal
employees are ineligible for copyright protection in the United States and are
licensed under GPLv3 elsewhere, while contractor contributions are copyrighted
and licensed under GPLv3. These assets carry no per-file authorship metadata, so
which case applies to any individual icon cannot be determined from the source
repository. They are therefore treated as GPLv3 throughout.

No TAK or ATAK branding is included. The branded assets in that repository
(atak_splash.png, ic_mil_atak_launcher.png and the *_atak_*
themed widgets) were deliberately excluded.

Mapping from CloudTAK menu key to ATAK-CIV asset name:

| Menu key | ATAK-CIV asset |
|---|---|
| `basemaps` | `nav_maps` |
| `channels` | `nav_channels` |
| `chats` | `nav_group_chat` |
| `connections` | `nav_radio` |
| `contacts` | `nav_contacts` |
| `features` | `nav_marker` |
| `files` | `nav_file` |
| `history` | `nav_track_history` |
| `iconsets` | `nav_gallery` |
| `imports` | `nav_import` |
| `missions` | `sync_original` |
| `overlays` | `nav_overlay_manager` |
| `packages` | `nav_data_package` |
| `routes` | `nav_routes` |
| `settings` | `nav_settings` |
| `videos` | `nav_video` |

Per-icon notes, the selection rationale and the audit of assets rejected as
unsuitable are in branding/atak-icons/MAPPING.md.

The Admin and COT Debugger menu entries retain their Tabler icons and are not
covered by this notice.


